WEBVTT

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:04.466
JIMMY:
[ <i>distorted</i> ]

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:07.597
<i>The aliens are</i>
<i>already among us.</i>

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.601
<i>Strange creatures with</i>

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:16.240
<i>unbelievable powers,</i>
<i>aliens are real,</i>

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.340
<i>but that isn't the</i>

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.009
<i>amazing part.</i>

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:20.848
<i>This is.</i>

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.182
<i>All of the creatures you�ve</i>

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.849
<i>just seen are actually alter</i>

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.017
<i>egos of one man.</i>

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:30.187
<i>His name is Ben Tennyson.</i>

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.696
You are so busted.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.346
[ birds chirping ]

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:02.159
That's not my best angle.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.557
[ glass breaking]

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:17.608
<i>Ugh!</i>

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.269
Every channel, Ben,
all weekend --

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.676
Nothing but you

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:22.738
wrecking things,
and they know who you are.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:26.110
Nobody cares if I'm a superhero!

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:27.744
Super menace.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:30.356
[ reporters shouting ]

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:34.052
[ camera shutters clicking ]

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.353
Okay, maybe a
few people care.

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.828
You should lie low for

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:42.493
a while,
maybe go to Julie's.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.161
Good idea, but how do

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:45.829
you get past them?

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.497
[ reporters shouting ]

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:52.011
[ camera shutters clicking ]

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.807
REPORTER:
Ben, Ben! Ben, Ben!

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.848
Ben, Ben, can I ask you a

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:56.847
question?

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.781
Do you have a statement?

00:01:58.852 --> 00:01:59.784
Yeah.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:03.619
It's hero time!

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.625
Humongousaur!

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:11.790
[ roaring ]

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:14.060
[ tires screeching ]

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.301
[ roaring ]

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:19.304
[ coughing ]

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.465
[ coughing ]

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.475
Hey, Gwen,
you got a lozenge?

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.977
Growing�s
rough on my throat.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.410
You should have used

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.606
one of your new ultimate

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:29.648
transformations.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:31.411
I wanted to scare <i>them,</i>

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.314
not <i>me.</i>

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.719
Thanks for letting
me hang out, Julie.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.155
I have to go to tennis

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.624
practice in an hour, but you can

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:41.955
stay here until I get back.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:43.791
[ <i>theme music plays</i> ]

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:44.921
Cable news?

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:47.125
Extra credit for
A.P. Current Events.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.867
Whoa, this guy hates you.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.130
Welcome back to the

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:52.398
<i>Will Harangue Nation.</i>

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.133
<i>Our top story --</i>
<i>it's got to be</i>

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.606
<i>Ben Tennyson,</i>
<i>16-year-old</i>

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.370
<i>High-School</i>
<i>student who�s been</i>

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.377
<i>outed as a one-man --</i>
<i>or should</i>

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:02.539
<i>I say ''boy''?</i>
<i>-- alien invasion.</i>

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:03.877
Why does everybody use

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:04.974
that picture?

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:06.712
You look cute.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:07.810
Really?

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.821
Yes, sweet and goofy.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:10.719
[ groans ]

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:11.722
[ giggles ]

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.258
HARANGUE:
Footage gathered over the

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.884
<i>past year,</i>
<i>but only now do we</i>

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.451
<i>understand</i>
<i>that all of these</i>

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:17.496
<i>seemingly unconnected</i>

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.394
<i>attacks...</i>

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.954
BEN:
''Attacks''?!

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.694
<i>HARANGUE:</i>
...were the work of

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:23.861
<i>Ben Tennyson</i>
<i>in his various</i>

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:26.132
<i>alien disguises</i>
<i>for who knows</i>

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:28.800
<i>what sinister purpose.</i>

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.399
How about saving the

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:31.704
whole entire universe?

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.211
How's that for
''sinister''?

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.940
Unbelievably,
some people

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:36.879
<i>defend the</i>
<i>actions of Tennyson,</i>

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.384
<i>claiming he's</i>
<i>some kind of Superhero.</i>

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.942
<i>obviously ridiculous, but</i>

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.544
<i>that's not for me to say.</i>

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.317
<i>No, I leave that to you, the</i>

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.948
<i>viewer, in tonight's poll,</i>

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:48.323
<i>''Ben Tennyson,</i>
<i>threat or menace?''</i>

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.861
<i>Call in with your vote.</i>

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.191
[ <i>theme music plays</i> ]

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.356
[ remote control beeps ]

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.524
[ television shuts off ]

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.067
It's too nice a day to

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.226
sit inside watching TV.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:57.530
Why don't we go for a drive in

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:58.434
your new car?

00:03:58.504 --> 00:03:59.596
That always cheers you up.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.196
I don't need cheering up.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:02.298
I'm not upset.

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:03.672
Why not?

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:04.903
Everybody hates you.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.446
BEN:
Maybe it's for the best.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.211
Maybe I can do
more good as a

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.048
public superhero
than I did in secret.

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:16.313
Sure,
most people think I'm a

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.219
menace now.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.882
Only 26% of adult

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.653
viewers think
you're a menace.

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:22.354
See? That's not bad.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.589
7 4% think you're a threat.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.097
But my point is, once

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:28.395
people get to know me,
I can win them over.

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.901
That hasn't been <i>my</i>

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.903
experience.

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:35.737
[ horn blaring ]

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.105
What's the emergency?

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:38.575
Sometimes I think the

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:40.078
only reason why
you guys used to

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:41.511
hang out with
me was because I

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.310
was the one
who could drive.

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:45.180
Well, maybe at first.

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:46.183
Ben!

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.776
While you guys have

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.412
been moping
around and hiding

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:50.820
from reporters,
I've been

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.881
working,
looking for a real problem.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:54.153
''Real problem''?

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:56.127
You know,
something we can hit.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:57.025
Ah.

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.461
I found the guy who

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.896
figured out
your secret I.D.,

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:01.900
then blabbed it all
over the internet.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.401
I say we go give
him a piece of

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.299
our mind.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:07.203
Best idea I've heard all day.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:09.707
[ siren wails ]

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:11.209
[ dog barks in distance ]

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:12.710
GWEN:
Julie is the only one

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:14.110
of us with any
common sense.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.011
She stayed back
in Bellwood.

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:18.175
That's what I just said.

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:20.884
[ electricity crackles ]

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.545
Oh!

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:23.646
Shh.

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:26.283
Why are we whispering,
anyway?

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:27.986
Because the guy in

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:29.460
there is the mastermind.

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:31.429
We got to be
ready for anything.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.024
What are you doing?

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:44.199
[ door creaks ]

00:05:48.915 --> 00:05:49.973
Oh.

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:53.541
You must be
friends of James'.

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:55.211
Jimmy!!

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:57.688
JIMMY:
I'm coming, Mom!

00:06:01.828 --> 00:06:03.887
That's your mastermind?

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:05.521
Ben Tennyson!

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:06.724
I'm Jimmy Jones.

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:08.232
Great to meet you.

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:22.546
Why did you do this to Ben?

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:24.810
I-I don't understand. Do what?

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:26.511
Ruin his life.

00:06:26.586 --> 00:06:27.814
I would never do

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.286
anything to hurt
Mr. Tennyson.

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:30.720
I'm a fan.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.087
[ gasps ]

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:33.591
GWEN:
That's enough, Kevin.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:37.595
Put him down
and let him talk.

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:39.654
Ugh!

00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:43.869
[ sobs ]

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:47.030
Dude, you are not gonna cry.

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:49.540
Stop being mean, Kevin,

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:50.541
seriously.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:53.374
Whatever.

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:55.778
[ sniffles ]

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:58.442
I'm sorry, Mr. Tennyson.

00:06:58.518 --> 00:06:59.951
[ nose blows ]

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:02.351
Why did you post that video?

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:06.859
Well, I run a website.

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:08.553
I collect
pictures of aliens

00:07:08.628 --> 00:07:11.096
that people have taken
all over the world.

00:07:11.164 --> 00:07:12.597
I noticed that
a lot of them

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:14.098
came from Bellwood.

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:16.294
So, I started
sorting the pictures.

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:18.030
Lots of them were
wearing this symbol.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.103
And you pieced together

00:07:21.174 --> 00:07:22.539
Ben's identity
from a picture of

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:24.269
him wearing
the omnitrix.

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:25.435
JIMMY:
Yeah.

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:26.808
I found stories
all over the

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:28.312
internet about
how you've helped

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:30.815
people and
saved the world.

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:32.316
I just thought
everybody should

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:33.647
know how
cool you are.

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:35.448
We know you were trying

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.216
to help, but by
revealing Ben's

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.882
secret, you've
made it harder

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:41.051
for him to help people.

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.890
JIMMY:
I'm sorry.

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:45.487
I thought you'd
like the fame.

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:47.931
You know,
all the attention and money?

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.126
Attention?

00:07:49.202 --> 00:07:51.466
Money?

00:07:51.537 --> 00:07:52.731
Why don't you show us

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:53.703
what you've learned?

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:55.035
I've got pictures of a

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:56.768
lot of your alien forms --

00:07:56.843 --> 00:07:58.606
Humongousaur,
Goop, Jeffrey.

00:07:58.678 --> 00:07:59.770
Jeffrey?

00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:01.677
You thought I
named one of my

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:02.839
aliens Jeffrey?

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:03.847
It's Jetray.

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:05.850
Hmm, that does make

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:06.885
more sense.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:11.750
Who is this one?

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:12.950
JIMMY:
I thought it was

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:13.855
Mr. Tennyson.

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:15.791
It just showed up
a few months ago.

00:08:15.862 --> 00:08:17.329
All of the sightings
have been

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:18.328
in Orlando.

00:08:18.397 --> 00:08:20.331
Hang on.
I've got some video.

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:22.060
[ beeping ]

00:08:26.372 --> 00:08:27.430
No sound?

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:30.032
I was lucky to get the pictures.

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:32.202
It's top secret.

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:33.267
Road trip?

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:35.473
We can borrow ship from Julie.

00:08:35.548 --> 00:08:36.810
Don't have to.

00:08:36.883 --> 00:08:38.316
We'll take the
rust bucket.

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:39.908
You want to drive all

00:08:39.986 --> 00:08:41.010
the way to Florida?

00:08:41.087 --> 00:08:42.714
Not <i>that</i> rust bucket.

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:44.983
The new one.

00:08:53.299 --> 00:08:55.961
Whoa!

00:08:59.038 --> 00:09:00.801
KEVIN:
Nice, huh?

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:02.738
It was a standard
plumber-issue

00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:04.298
ship,
but I've made some

00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:05.537
improvements.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.245
BEN:
Specs?

00:09:13.386 --> 00:09:14.910
Supersonic in

00:09:14.987 --> 00:09:16.955
atmosphere,
subspace hyperdrive

00:09:17.023 --> 00:09:19.457
for effective FTL,
bonus gizmos

00:09:19.525 --> 00:09:21.550
I've acquired here and there.

00:09:21.627 --> 00:09:22.719
Sweet.

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:24.422
This is going to
be the coolest

00:09:24.497 --> 00:09:25.623
thing I ever crashed.

00:09:25.698 --> 00:09:27.029
Extranet access.

00:09:27.099 --> 00:09:28.726
We can use our
Plumbers' badges

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:30.462
to access any
database on Earth,

00:09:30.536 --> 00:09:32.163
even secure ones.

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:33.762
Bor-ing!

00:09:33.839 --> 00:09:35.329
Make it go.

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:44.778
GWEN:
I found the source of

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.681
the video --
Security cameras in

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:48.344
a top-secret NASA facility.

00:09:48.421 --> 00:09:50.753
I'm sending you
the coordinates, Kevin.

00:09:50.823 --> 00:09:51.721
Got them.

00:09:51.791 --> 00:09:53.418
We'll be there in two minutes.

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:54.982
According to this,

00:09:55.061 --> 00:09:56.585
they're building a Starship.

00:09:56.662 --> 00:09:57.754
About time.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:59.320
Earth tech is so
primitive, I'm

00:09:59.398 --> 00:10:01.730
embarrassed to tell
my friends I'm from here.

00:10:01.801 --> 00:10:03.132
[ beeping ]

00:10:03.202 --> 00:10:04.032
Trouble.

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:05.627
We're flying into restricted

00:10:05.705 --> 00:10:06.694
airspace.

00:10:13.212 --> 00:10:14.543
Incoming!

00:10:16.215 --> 00:10:18.581
This is a
brand-new paint job!

00:10:26.492 --> 00:10:27.390
Kevin!

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:28.950
Those guys are on our side!

00:10:29.028 --> 00:10:30.393
You can't shoot at them!

00:10:30.463 --> 00:10:31.760
No harm done.

00:10:31.831 --> 00:10:33.594
He ejected,
and his parachute is

00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:36.760
only a little on fire.

00:10:36.836 --> 00:10:38.326
Open it.

00:10:43.376 --> 00:10:46.539
Jetray!

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:55.450
He's gone!

00:10:55.521 --> 00:10:56.852
I don't see him, either.

00:10:56.922 --> 00:10:59.083
I -- there he is!

00:11:07.767 --> 00:11:09.428
JETRAY:
Gotcha!

00:11:14.273 --> 00:11:17.606
Um, take me
to your leader?

00:11:19.779 --> 00:11:21.212
If you so much as twitch,

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:22.542
you're going down.

00:11:22.615 --> 00:11:24.776
Whoa, whoa, easy, guys.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:26.215
I'm the famous

00:11:26.285 --> 00:11:27.149
Ben Tennyson.

00:11:27.219 --> 00:11:28.481
I'm a superhero.

00:11:28.554 --> 00:11:30.351
You have heard of me, right?

00:11:31.223 --> 00:11:32.155
[ bars slam ]

00:11:34.093 --> 00:11:35.651
I'm pretty sure
I'm supposed to

00:11:35.728 --> 00:11:37.525
get a phone call!

00:11:39.732 --> 00:11:41.563
Let him out.

00:11:45.471 --> 00:11:47.735
How did you...

00:11:47.807 --> 00:11:49.274
We showed him these.

00:11:49.341 --> 00:11:50.865
Even though
the Plumbers are

00:11:50.943 --> 00:11:52.308
secret,
every government on

00:11:52.378 --> 00:11:53.970
Earth recognizes
your authority

00:11:54.046 --> 00:11:54.978
in these matters.

00:11:55.047 --> 00:11:56.514
Turns out NASA has a

00:11:56.582 --> 00:11:57.412
problem.

00:11:57.483 --> 00:11:59.576
A problem I understand is

00:11:59.652 --> 00:12:00.949
right up your alley.

00:12:09.762 --> 00:12:11.593
It's called the Orion.

00:12:11.664 --> 00:12:14.224
It's capable of traveling at 15%

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:15.392
of the speed of light.

00:12:15.468 --> 00:12:16.901
[ whistles ]
How?

00:12:16.969 --> 00:12:18.334
Nuclear pulse drive.

00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:19.928
Once clear of the Earth, a

00:12:20.005 --> 00:12:21.768
series of
atomic bombs explode,

00:12:21.841 --> 00:12:24.002
propelling it through space.

00:12:24.076 --> 00:12:25.202
Whoa.

00:12:25.277 --> 00:12:26.767
We've been
building her for

00:12:26.846 --> 00:12:27.676
over 50 years.

00:12:27.747 --> 00:12:29.044
But now,
only months from

00:12:29.115 --> 00:12:30.343
completion,
a series of

00:12:30.416 --> 00:12:32.646
robberies has
practically shut us down.

00:12:32.718 --> 00:12:33.912
Robberies?

00:12:33.986 --> 00:12:35.578
A creature
comes in here

00:12:35.654 --> 00:12:37.417
every night and
steals pieces of

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:38.320
the ship.

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:40.290
Nothing we've
tried can stop it.

00:12:40.359 --> 00:12:42.293
I'm hoping maybe
you people will

00:12:42.361 --> 00:12:43.794
have more luck.

00:13:05.718 --> 00:13:08.186
ULTIMATRIX:
Uncataloged DNA detected.

00:13:08.254 --> 00:13:10.381
<i>Function not available.</i>

00:13:10.456 --> 00:13:11.548
<i>Please stand by.</i>

00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:14.218
[ beeping ]

00:13:14.293 --> 00:13:16.227
<i>Function not available.</i>

00:13:16.295 --> 00:13:18.229
<i>Please stand by.</i>

00:13:18.297 --> 00:13:20.561
KEVIN:
We can't let you leave

00:13:20.633 --> 00:13:22.100
unless you
show us a receipt.

00:13:32.878 --> 00:13:34.505
Who are you?

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:36.013
What do you --

00:13:42.721 --> 00:13:45.485
BEN:
Hey! Seafood salad!

00:13:45.558 --> 00:13:47.150
Over here!

00:13:47.226 --> 00:13:49.820
[ screams ]

00:13:54.967 --> 00:13:57.060
That worked a lot
better in my head.

00:13:58.137 --> 00:14:00.731
BIVALVAN:
[ snarling ]

00:14:00.806 --> 00:14:02.899
ULTIMATRIX:
<i>Function not available.</i>

00:14:02.975 --> 00:14:04.237
<i>Please stand by.</i>

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:05.572
[ beeping ]

00:14:05.644 --> 00:14:07.236
Oh, man!

00:14:12.618 --> 00:14:13.448
[ beeping ]

00:14:13.519 --> 00:14:14.781
I don't suppose you want

00:14:14.854 --> 00:14:16.287
to talk about this?

00:14:16.355 --> 00:14:18.687
Ugh!

00:14:25.364 --> 00:14:27.127
ULTIMATRIX:
<i>Unknown DNA sample acquired.</i>

00:14:27.199 --> 00:14:29.326
<i>Scan complete.</i>

00:14:30.803 --> 00:14:33.567
What did you do?

00:14:33.639 --> 00:14:35.573
Oh, <i>now</i> you want to talk.

00:14:35.641 --> 00:14:37.165
[ beeping ]

00:14:46.252 --> 00:14:49.016
Chromastone!

00:14:49.088 --> 00:14:50.350
Wasn't even sure I still had

00:14:50.422 --> 00:14:51.753
this one.

00:14:58.564 --> 00:15:00.498
[ electricity crackles ]

00:15:00.566 --> 00:15:04.502
[ screams ]

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:06.231
Ugh!

00:15:17.816 --> 00:15:21.081
Ben, are you okay?

00:15:22.488 --> 00:15:24.251
[ groans ]

00:15:24.323 --> 00:15:27.258
We've got a big problem, son.

00:15:27.326 --> 00:15:29.123
The first few
times that thing

00:15:29.194 --> 00:15:30.559
came in here,
it stole

00:15:30.629 --> 00:15:32.324
shielding,
a control system,

00:15:32.398 --> 00:15:33.558
timing sequencers.

00:15:33.632 --> 00:15:34.724
But this time?

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:36.734
This time he took the engine.

00:15:36.802 --> 00:15:38.235
And by engine, you

00:15:38.304 --> 00:15:39.566
mean...

00:15:39.638 --> 00:15:42.801
A nuclear bomb. Yes.

00:15:45.577 --> 00:15:47.374
[ beeping ]
Come on, guys, anything?

00:15:47.446 --> 00:15:48.572
You've been at this for --

00:15:48.647 --> 00:15:49.909
KEVIN:
15 minutes.

00:15:49.982 --> 00:15:51.415
And, yeah,
we found the bomb.

00:15:51.483 --> 00:15:52.882
It looks like it's underwater.

00:15:52.952 --> 00:15:54.783
I can get us there.

00:16:36.495 --> 00:16:38.087
Now I get it.

00:16:38.163 --> 00:16:39.858
He's doing the
same thing <i>you</i>

00:16:39.932 --> 00:16:41.024
always do, Kevin.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:43.091
Stealing?

00:16:48.273 --> 00:16:50.298
I think he's just trying

00:16:50.376 --> 00:16:51.741
to fix up his ship.

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:53.402
Am I right?

00:16:53.479 --> 00:16:54.741
You are correct.

00:16:54.813 --> 00:16:56.280
Now leave me be.

00:16:56.348 --> 00:16:58.908
I want to go home,
and I am two

00:16:58.984 --> 00:17:00.008
minutes from launch.

00:17:04.390 --> 00:17:05.254
GWEN:
If you launch your

00:17:05.324 --> 00:17:06.848
ship, the explosion will destroy

00:17:06.925 --> 00:17:08.051
all of Central Florida.

00:17:08.127 --> 00:17:10.357
I'm not sure I see your point.

00:17:10.429 --> 00:17:11.794
Killing a couple

00:17:11.864 --> 00:17:13.195
million people isn't cool.

00:17:13.265 --> 00:17:14.698
We can't let you do it.

00:17:14.767 --> 00:17:16.029
Also, there's some

00:17:16.101 --> 00:17:17.864
good theme parks here.

00:17:17.936 --> 00:17:19.198
You would stand

00:17:19.271 --> 00:17:21.535
in my way?

00:17:22.975 --> 00:17:24.340
That cable's live.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:25.775
If I drop the shield,

00:17:25.844 --> 00:17:26.936
it'll fry us.

00:17:27.012 --> 00:17:28.274
[ beeping ]

00:17:28.347 --> 00:17:30.941
Spidermonkey!

00:17:32.017 --> 00:17:34.781
Don't touch it.

00:17:34.853 --> 00:17:36.150
Stop the clam guy.

00:17:36.221 --> 00:17:37.415
We'll think of something.

00:17:37.489 --> 00:17:38.922
We will?

00:17:38.991 --> 00:17:40.253
A face full of

00:17:40.325 --> 00:17:42.816
web ought to
slow you down.

00:17:43.629 --> 00:17:45.324
Whoa! Whoa!

00:17:47.232 --> 00:17:49.166
There is nothing

00:17:49.234 --> 00:17:52.169
you can do to stop me.

00:17:53.639 --> 00:17:55.402
SPIDERMONKEY:
Maybe not me...

00:17:55.474 --> 00:17:57.237
But my new
Ultimatrix comes

00:17:57.309 --> 00:17:58.799
with some new features.

00:17:58.877 --> 00:18:00.811
There's a time to go hero, and

00:18:00.879 --> 00:18:02.710
there's a time to go ultimate!

00:18:09.955 --> 00:18:12.788
Ultimate Spidermonkey!

00:18:12.858 --> 00:18:14.485
[ roars ]

00:18:29.675 --> 00:18:31.609
Give up?

00:18:31.677 --> 00:18:33.702
Why should I?

00:18:42.287 --> 00:18:44.517
The bomb!

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:45.784
KEVIN:
Got it!

00:18:45.858 --> 00:18:47.792
10 seconds to spare.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:50.192
You did that on purpose.

00:18:53.432 --> 00:18:55.366
You okay?

00:18:55.434 --> 00:18:56.867
Y-yeah, that's a little

00:18:56.935 --> 00:18:58.368
different.

00:18:58.437 --> 00:19:00.029
Time for you to start talking.

00:19:00.105 --> 00:19:02.369
Let's start with a name.

00:19:02.441 --> 00:19:04.466
I am Bivalvan.

00:19:04.543 --> 00:19:06.738
I come from a small planet in

00:19:06.812 --> 00:19:09.542
what you call the
Andromeda Galaxy.

00:19:09.615 --> 00:19:11.549
Long way from home.

00:19:11.617 --> 00:19:13.380
What brings you here?

00:19:13.452 --> 00:19:14.714
I was kidnapped,

00:19:14.786 --> 00:19:16.879
along with four others, by a

00:19:16.955 --> 00:19:19.389
monster named Aggregor.

00:19:19.458 --> 00:19:22.552
We managed to
escape him but

00:19:22.628 --> 00:19:24.892
crashed here
on your planet.

00:19:24.963 --> 00:19:26.555
Where are the others?

00:19:26.632 --> 00:19:27.894
I don't know.

00:19:27.966 --> 00:19:29.558
We were separated.

00:19:29.635 --> 00:19:31.262
Four aliens that aren't

00:19:31.336 --> 00:19:32.360
in the Ultimatrix.

00:19:32.437 --> 00:19:33.870
That's pretty cool.

00:19:33.939 --> 00:19:36.271
Don't worry about your friends.

00:19:36.341 --> 00:19:38.104
We'll find them
and get them all

00:19:38.177 --> 00:19:39.166
a ride back home.

00:19:39.244 --> 00:19:41.872
And...what about me?

00:19:41.947 --> 00:19:43.209
Same deal.

00:19:43.282 --> 00:19:44.806
I'll call the Plumbers.

00:19:44.883 --> 00:19:45.815
They'll take you.

00:19:45.884 --> 00:19:48.318
KEVIN:
[ grunting ]

00:19:48.387 --> 00:19:49.479
[ electricity crackles ]

00:19:49.555 --> 00:19:51.079
We'll make sure the

00:19:51.156 --> 00:19:52.487
bomb gets back to NASA.

00:19:52.558 --> 00:19:53.820
Not that we don't

00:19:53.892 --> 00:19:56.383
trust you, but we don't.

00:20:02.801 --> 00:20:05.065
JULIE:
You have to go in

00:20:05.137 --> 00:20:06.069
sometime.

00:20:06.138 --> 00:20:07.571
I could drop out.

00:20:07.639 --> 00:20:08.970
Last night, you were

00:20:09.041 --> 00:20:10.338
two feet from
an atomic bomb.

00:20:10.409 --> 00:20:12.343
You can't be scared of
your classmates.

00:20:12.411 --> 00:20:13.639
Everybody knows my

00:20:13.712 --> 00:20:14.542
secret, Julie.

00:20:14.613 --> 00:20:16.012
And if they've
been watching

00:20:16.081 --> 00:20:18.072
the news,
everybody hates me.

00:20:25.457 --> 00:20:28.790
Not everybody.

00:20:55.287 --> 00:20:58.222
[ applause ]

00:21:01.727 --> 00:21:03.024
You've helped a lot of people

00:21:03.095 --> 00:21:03.925
in this school.

00:21:03.996 --> 00:21:05.657
You're all right, Tennyson.

00:21:14.406 --> 00:21:16.101
Hello?

00:21:16.174 --> 00:21:18.005
Are you the Plumbers?

00:21:18.076 --> 00:21:20.636
Ben said you'd
be here quickly,

00:21:20.712 --> 00:21:22.236
but I didn't think...

00:21:25.217 --> 00:21:26.650
Aggregor!

00:21:26.718 --> 00:21:29.152
No one escapes me,

00:21:29.221 --> 00:21:32.486
Bivalvan.

00:21:32.557 --> 00:21:33.649
[ electricity crackles ]

00:21:33.725 --> 00:21:35.625
BIVALVAN:
[ screams ]
